1a:I[28440,["2619","static/chunks/2619-04bc32f026a0d946.js?dpl=dpl_7RkrhxkHMBxRwELcvSCn238CEijs","6489","static/chunks/6489-699922ea493f9867.js?dpl=dpl_7RkrhxkHMBxRwELcvSCn238CEijs","1356","static/chunks/1356-9e2757ba007ad1f9.js?dpl=dpl_7RkrhxkHMBxRwELcvSCn238CEijs","951","static/chunks/951-3dbda3a86d4c6444.js?dpl=dpl_7RkrhxkHMBxRwELcvSCn238CEijs","2799","static/chunks/2799-ce430b82b11995d5.js?dpl=dpl_7RkrhxkHMBxRwELcvSCn238CEijs","6589","static/chunks/6589-cfdc115b042e146b.js?dpl=dpl_7RkrhxkHMBxRwELcvSCn238CEijs","3650","static/chunks/3650-106e80ed926f59bf.js?dpl=dpl_7RkrhxkHMBxRwELcvSCn238CEijs","8440","static/chunks/8440-bfb72547be677d52.js?dpl=dpl_7RkrhxkHMBxRwELcvSCn238CEijs","134","static/chunks/app/%5Bpattern%5D/%5BproblemId%5D/page-f9e02a54f5641ad9.js?dpl=dpl_7RkrhxkHMBxRwELcvSCn238CEijs"],"AnimationRunner"]
19:["$","$L1a","word-ladder",{"problem":{"id":"word-ladder","patternId":"graphs","title":"Word Ladder","subtitle":"Shortest transformation sequence via BFS","kind":"problem","leetcode":{"id":127,"slug":"word-ladder","difficulty":"Hard"},"companies":["Amazon","Google","Meta"],"statement":"Given beginWord, endWord and a word list, return the length of the shortest transformation sequence from beginWord to endWord, changing one letter at a time, where every intermediate word is in the list (or 0 if impossible).","input":[],"render":"graph","approaches":[{"label":"Words as a graph + BFS for the shortest ladder","complexity":{"time":"O(N · L · 26)","space":"O(N · L)"},"pseudocode":["build graph: edge(a, b) if a, b differ by one letter","queue = [beginWord]; dist[beginWord] = 1; visited = {beginWord}","while queue: u = queue.pop_front()           // dequeue (level order)","    for v in neighbours(u):","        if v in visited: continue            // already shortest","        dist[v] = dist[u] + 1; enqueue v      // first time = shortest","    if u == endWord: return dist[u]           // BFS ⇒ shortest ladder","return 0                                       // unreachable"],"steps":[{"codeLine":1,"narration":"Word Ladder (LeetCode 127): transform \"hit\" into \"cog\", changing ONE letter at a time, and every intermediate word must be in the word list. Model it as a GRAPH, each word is a node, and an edge joins two words that differ by exactly one letter. The answer is the SHORTEST ladder length (count of words on the path). Shortest path on an unweighted graph = BFS.","graph":{"nodes":[{"id":"hit","label":"hit","x":0,"y":2},{"id":"hot","label":"hot","x":1.4,"y":2},{"id":"dot","label":"dot","x":2.8,"y":1},{"id":"lot","label":"lot","x":2.8,"y":3},{"id":"dog","label":"dog","x":4.2,"y":1},{"id":"log","label":"log","x":4.2,"y":3},{"id":"cog","label":"cog","x":5.6,"y":2}],"edges":[{"from":"hit","to":"hot"},{"from":"hot","to":"dot"},{"from":"hot","to":"lot"},{"from":"dot","to":"dog"},{"from":"dot","to":"lot"},{"from":"lot","to":"log"},{"from":"dog","to":"log"},{"from":"dog","to":"cog"},{"from":"log","to":"cog"}],"activeId":"$undefined","visitedIds":[],"frontierIds":[],"notes":{},"queue":[],"queueLabel":"BFS queue","label":"word graph (one-letter edges)"},"vars":[["begin","hit"],["end","cog"],["goal","fewest words"]]},{"codeLine":2,"narration":"Seed the BFS: enqueue \"hit\" at level 1 and mark it visited. The level on each node = number of words in the shortest ladder from \"hit\" to it. BFS expands the queue level by level, so distances only ever grow.","graph":{"nodes":"$19:props:problem:approaches:0:steps:0:graph:nodes","edges":"$19:props:problem:approaches:0:steps:0:graph:edges","activeId":"$undefined","visitedIds":["hit"],"frontierIds":["hit"],"notes":{"hit":"1"},"queue":[{"label":"hit","sub":"lvl 1"}],"queueLabel":"BFS queue","label":"word graph (one-letter edges)","highlightIds":["hit"]},"vars":[["queue","hit"],["dist[hit]",1]]},{"codeLine":3,"narration":"Dequeue \"hit\" (level 1). Because BFS pulls words in non-decreasing level order, the first time we ever reach a word is along a shortest ladder, so dist[\"hit\"] = 1 is final. Now scan its one-letter neighbours.","graph":{"nodes":"$19:props:problem:approaches:0:steps:0:graph:nodes","edges":"$19:props:problem:approaches:0:steps:0:graph:edges","activeId":"hit","visitedIds":["hit"],"frontierIds":[],"notes":{"hit":"1"},"queue":[],"queueLabel":"BFS queue","label":"word graph (one-letter edges)","highlightIds":["hit"]},"vars":[["dequeue","hit"],["level","1"],["queue left",0]]},{"codeLine":5,"narration":"\"hit\" → \"hot\" differs by one letter and \"hot\" is unvisited. Enqueue \"hot\" at level 2 and record its parent as \"hit\". The highlighted edge is the step we just took in the ladder.","graph":{"nodes":"$19:props:problem:approaches:0:steps:0:graph:nodes","edges":"$19:props:problem:approaches:0:steps:0:graph:edges","activeId":"hit","visitedIds":["hit","hot"],"frontierIds":["hot"],"notes":{"hit":"1","hot":"2"},"queue":[{"label":"hot","sub":"lvl 2"}],"queueLabel":"BFS queue","label":"word graph (one-letter edges)","highlightIds":["hot"],"edgeHighlights":[["hit","hot"]]},"vars":[["neighbour","hot"],["dist","2"],["parent","hit"],["enqueue","hot"]]},{"codeLine":3,"narration":"Dequeue \"hot\" (level 2). Because BFS pulls words in non-decreasing level order, the first time we ever reach a word is along a shortest ladder, so dist[\"hot\"] = 2 is final. Now scan its one-letter neighbours.","graph":{"nodes":"$19:props:problem:approaches:0:steps:0:graph:nodes","edges":"$19:props:problem:approaches:0:steps:0:graph:edges","activeId":"hot","visitedIds":["hit","hot"],"frontierIds":[],"notes":{"hit":"1","hot":"2"},"queue":[],"queueLabel":"BFS queue","label":"word graph (one-letter edges)","highlightIds":["hot"]},"vars":[["dequeue","hot"],["level","2"],["queue left",0]]},{"codeLine":4,"narration":"\"hit\" is already visited (reached earlier at level 1, an equal-or-shorter ladder) → skip it. Re-enqueuing would only find a same-or-longer path, never a better one.","graph":{"nodes":"$19:props:problem:approaches:0:steps:0:graph:nodes","edges":"$19:props:problem:approaches:0:steps:0:graph:edges","activeId":"hot","visitedIds":["hit","hot"],"frontierIds":[],"notes":{"hit":"1","hot":"2"},"queue":[],"queueLabel":"BFS queue","label":"word graph (one-letter edges)","highlightIds":["hit"],"edgeHighlights":[["hot","hit"]]},"vars":[["neighbour","hit"],["seen at","1"],["action","skip"]]},{"codeLine":5,"narration":"\"hot\" → \"dot\" differs by one letter and \"dot\" is unvisited. Enqueue \"dot\" at level 3 and record its parent as \"hot\". The highlighted edge is the step we just took in the ladder.","graph":{"nodes":"$19:props:problem:approaches:0:steps:0:graph:nodes","edges":"$19:props:problem:approaches:0:steps:0:graph:edges","activeId":"hot","visitedIds":["hit","hot","dot"],"frontierIds":["dot"],"notes":{"hit":"1","hot":"2","dot":"3"},"queue":[{"label":"dot","sub":"lvl 3"}],"queueLabel":"BFS queue","label":"word graph (one-letter edges)","highlightIds":["dot"],"edgeHighlights":[["hot","dot"]]},"vars":[["neighbour","dot"],["dist","3"],["parent","hot"],["enqueue","dot"]]},{"codeLine":5,"narration":"\"hot\" → \"lot\" differs by one letter and \"lot\" is unvisited. Enqueue \"lot\" at level 3 and record its parent as \"hot\". The highlighted edge is the step we just took in the ladder.","graph":{"nodes":"$19:props:problem:approaches:0:steps:0:graph:nodes","edges":"$19:props:problem:approaches:0:steps:0:graph:edges","activeId":"hot","visitedIds":["hit","hot","dot","lot"],"frontierIds":["dot","lot"],"notes":{"hit":"1","hot":"2","dot":"3","lot":"3"},"queue":[{"label":"dot","sub":"lvl 3"},{"label":"lot","sub":"lvl 3"}],"queueLabel":"BFS queue","label":"word graph (one-letter edges)","highlightIds":["lot"],"edgeHighlights":[["hot","lot"]]},"vars":[["neighbour","lot"],["dist","3"],["parent","hot"],["enqueue","lot"]]},{"codeLine":3,"narration":"Dequeue \"dot\" (level 3). Because BFS pulls words in non-decreasing level order, the first time we ever reach a word is along a shortest ladder, so dist[\"dot\"] = 3 is final. Now scan its one-letter neighbours.","graph":{"nodes":"$19:props:problem:approaches:0:steps:0:graph:nodes","edges":"$19:props:problem:approaches:0:steps:0:graph:edges","activeId":"dot","visitedIds":["hit","hot","dot","lot"],"frontierIds":["lot"],"notes":{"hit":"1","hot":"2","dot":"3","lot":"3"},"queue":[{"label":"lot","sub":"lvl 3"}],"queueLabel":"BFS queue","label":"word graph (one-letter edges)","highlightIds":["dot"]},"vars":[["dequeue","dot"],["level","3"],["queue left",1]]},{"codeLine":4,"narration":"\"hot\" is already visited (reached earlier at level 2, an equal-or-shorter ladder) → skip it. Re-enqueuing would only find a same-or-longer path, never a better one.","graph":{"nodes":"$19:props:problem:approaches:0:steps:0:graph:nodes","edges":"$19:props:problem:approaches:0:steps:0:graph:edges","activeId":"dot","visitedIds":["hit